.TH ROLLING_MA 8 "2026-11-20" "rolling-linux 2.1.11" "Rolling WWAN Services Manual"
.SH NAME
rolling_ma \- ModemManager FCC unlock helper for Rolling Wireless WWAN devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/bin/rolling_ma
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rolling_ma
performs the FCC unlock flow for Rolling Wireless WWAN modems (for
example the PCI device 14c3:4d75).  It is not meant to be run by hand:
.BR ModemManager (8)
invokes it automatically through the shipped FCC unlock scripts when
a modem is detected as FCC\-locked.
.PP
The shipped scripts under
.I /usr/share/linux\-apps/rolling_ma_service/fcc\-unlock.d
dispatch on the DMI machine vendor: Dell machines run
.BR rolling_ma ;
Lenovo machines are unlocked by an external vendor tool.
The scripts are linked into
.I /usr/lib/x86_64\-linux\-gnu/ModemManager/fcc\-unlock.d
for each supported USB/PCI modem ID; ModemManager calls them when the
modem reports the FCC lock state.
.SH OPTIONS
.B rolling_ma
takes no command\-line options; it is invoked by ModemManager through
the shipped FCC unlock scripts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/linux\-apps/rolling_ma_service/fcc\-unlock.d/
Shipped FCC unlock scripts (one per supported modem ID).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/x86_64\-linux\-gnu/ModemManager/fcc\-unlock.d/
ModemManager FCC unlock lookup directory; the shipped scripts are
linked into it by the package post\-install script.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ModemManager (8),
.BR rolling_helper (8),
.BR rolling_config (8),
.BR rolling_flash (8)
